      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your argument effectively hinges on a \"trolley problem\" framework where the immediate economic pain is a justification for a deceptively greater long-term survival benefit. You should emphasize that the cost of inaction—climate-induced displacement and catastrophic economic collapse far exceeds the initial transition costs. To strengthen your case, include the fact that modern policy can mitigate short-term price spikes through strategic investment in social safety nets rather than abandoning vulnerable populations. Ultimately, frame the transition not as a binary choice between climate and economy, but as the only sustainable path where future economic stability is actually more valuable than present comfort.\n\nI strongly encourage you to explicitly address counterarguments about job losses and inflation in specific demographic sections to ensure your thesis remains robust. Including concrete data on how much the alternative cost to global GDP would be over the next 50 years will provide a powerful quantitative backing to your qualitative claims.",
